# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Claude Code local settings + tool artifacts (never commit to this public repo)
# — everything under .claude/ is ignored EXCEPT shared project settings, team
# rules, the upstream-check skill, and the codebase map (tracked so sessions and CI share one map;
# without the negation, git add warns and agents wrongly conclude it is
# local-only). settings.local.json (per-machine overrides) stays ignored.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/rules/
!.claude/rules/**
!.claude/.codebase-info/
!.claude/.codebase-info/**
!.claude/skills/
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/upstream-check/
!.claude/skills/upstream-check/**
.playwright-mcp/

# Node (only relevant if a plugin ever adds tooling)
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Logs
*.log
.sq-shots/

# Playwright MCP session artifacts and ad-hoc verification captures
.playwright-mcp/
/*.png

# Local-only Windows Sandbox clean-room harness (maintainer tooling, not published)
/sandbox/

# live-rules: personal rules, not shared
.claude/rules/*.local.md

# graphify knowledge graph (codebase-mapper graph mode). The graph summary and
# the graph itself travel with the repo, because `graphify query|explain|path`
# read them and a clone must be able to answer structure questions without
# rebuilding. Everything else graphify writes — graph.html, the extraction
# cache, the manifest, memory/ — is local build output.
/graphify-out/*
!/graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md
!/graphify-out/graph.json
